# Whitelist-style .gitignore.
#
# Everything is ignored by default. Anything you want tracked must be
# added with `!` below. This keeps the repo immune to accidental commits
# of editor swap files, OS metadata, downloaded blobs, secrets, and
# transient artefacts. The trade-off is explicit: if a new file type
# appears in the repo, you must whitelist it intentionally.
#
# Pattern (verified working pattern, see git's gitignore docs):
#
#   *              # ignore every name at every depth, but still descend
#   .*             # ignore every dotfile at every depth
#   !/<file>       # re-allow a specific file at the repo root
#   !/<dir>/       # re-allow a specific directory entry at the root
#   !/<dir>/**     # re-allow everything inside that directory recursively
#
# Do NOT use `/*` as the top-level blacklist: it anchors to the root
# and prevents git from descending into directories to evaluate the
# whitelist, which silently re-ignores everything.

# --- Blacklist ---------------------------------------------------------

# Ignore every name at every depth. Descends into directories (so
# `!/dir/**` rules below can match), but matches names.
*

# Ignore dotfiles at every depth.
.*

# --- Whitelist: top-level files ----------------------------------------

!/LICENSE
!/README.md

# --- Whitelist: top-level directories ----------------------------------

!/config/
!/config/**

!/deploy/
!/deploy/**

!/docs/
!/docs/**

!/scripts/
!/scripts/**

!/tests/
!/tests/**

!/models/
!/models/**

# --- Whitelist: dotfiles at the root -----------------------------------

!/.gitignore
!/.editorconfig